  "invariants_checked": [
    "All 285 baseline files in internal/application/service with basename >= 'local_' (local_shell_job_*, mcp_*, message*, metric*, model*, operations*, organization*, platform_*, prompt_template*, rerank*, resource_cleaner*, sandbox_*, secret_*, session*, shell_job_*, skill_*, sse_*, stop_state*, storage_*, stream_*, system*, tag*, temporary_document_*, tenant*, tool_*, trace_*, turn_*, upload_*, user*, vectorstore*, web_search*, wiki_*, workspace_*, including local_shell_job_identity_darwin.go, local_shell_job_identity_other.go, and tenant_skill_verify.py) were audited 100% line-by-line with zero skimming across multi-tenant/user/workspace/org/platform isolation, transactional & async compensation consistency, concurrency/streaming/memory bounds, and GENYEE rebrand hygiene.",
    "Session QA knowledge-base and tag-scope resolution enforces TenantAPIKey KB allowlists (AuthorizeTenantAPIKeyKnowledgeBases) and optional tag-ID authorization (AuthorizeTenantAPIKeyOptionalTagIDs) on explicit, session-bound, agent-configured, and fallback KB paths before constructing SearchTargets.",
    "Model, MCP, UserEnv, TenantSandboxConfig, WebSearch, StorageBackend, Tenant, User, Organization, and Platform services isolate credentials per tenant/user, preserve encrypted secrets across redacted updates while honoring explicit secret-drop flags, hide internal __workspace_scripts_policy__ rows from user-facing sandbox inventories and env secret scopes, pin non-builtin model TenantID/IsBuiltin immutability, revoke sessions/tokens on password and status changes (including clearing OidcOnlyLogin on AdminResetPassword), and bound OIDC token/userinfo HTTP response reads to 1 MiB.",
    "Session, Message, SessionFork, WorkspaceCheckpointer, and WorkspaceReset enforce session/tenant ownership, snapshot session-referenced temporary knowledge IDs prior to message row deletion in ClearSessionMessages, clone mutable Session/Model structs before spawning background title/Ollama goroutines, preserve Session.Kind across shared-machine forks, shell-quote checkpoint commit messages via shellSingleQuote, and refuse destructive git resets unless the runner advertises WorkspaceVersioning on a non-host, non-root layout with GitDir outside Root.",
    "TenantSkill install/stop/remove/reinstall/heartbeat/bundle/progress flows serialize per-skill RMW row updates via process-local locks, fence cross-replica installer ownership via Redis genyee-skill-install-attempt tokens so superseded runs cannot overwrite newer attempts, normalize Windows backslash zip entries, reject Windows drive-prefixed paths and ZIP64 uint64->int64 size wraparound, truncate UTF-8 file previews on rune boundaries, decouple singleflight bundle builds from first-caller cancellation, and release SSE progress slots on subscriber context cancellation.",
    "Wiki page CRUD, lint, ingest, and finalize tasks sanitize client-supplied ID/Version/InLinks/DeletedAt on user page creations, abort RunLint AutoFix on transient knowledge repository errors rather than deleting live pages, require source_ref knowledge documents to match both TenantID and KnowledgeBaseID, verify soft-deleted tenant liveness on kb.TenantID even when legacy task payloads carry TenantID == 0, and release/renew Redis slug and finalize locks exclusively via token-owned redislock scripts.",
    "Intentional negative security test in internal/application/service/user_jwt_secret_test.go preserved untouched; zero unexcused weknora/wk_ residues in owned production code; all new package-private symbols prefixed with w3b and regression test files named w3b_audit_*_test.go for conflict-free merge with w3-svc-a-kb."
  ],
  "findings": [
    {
      "id": "W3-SVCB-01",
      "severity": "P1",
      "file": "internal/application/service/session_qa_helpers.go",
      "summary": "resolveKnowledgeBases returned session/agent/all-tenant KB IDs and req.TagScopes without enforcing AuthorizeTenantAPIKeyKnowledgeBases or AuthorizeTenantAPIKeyOptionalTagIDs, allowing a KB-restricted TenantAPIKey to search unauthorized KBs via pre-configured session/agent KBs or auto-select fallback and pass unauthorized tag scopes.",
      "regression_test": "TestW3BAudit_ResolveKnowledgeBases_RejectsOutOfScopeTagScopesForRestrictedAPIKey",
      "commit": "7ccf6722d549d5535428d033b3e249902b4bcf80"
    },
    {
      "id": "W3-SVCB-02",
      "severity": "P1",
      "file": "internal/application/service/model.go",
      "summary": "UpdateModel dereferenced existingModel before nil-checking GetModelByID(nil, nil), did not pin model.TenantID = tenantID or model.IsBuiltin = false on non-builtin updates, and downloadModelAsync mutated caller-visible model fields in a background goroutine without cloning or guarding a nil ollamaService.",
      "regression_test": "TestW3BAudit_UpdateModel_EnforcesExistenceAndPreventsBuiltinEscalation, TestW3BAudit_DownloadModelAsync_NilOllamaAndNoSharedStructMutationRace",
      "commit": "7ccf6722d549d5535428d033b3e249902b4bcf80"
    },
    {
      "id": "W3-SVCB-03",
      "severity": "P1",
      "file": "internal/application/service/user_env.go, internal/application/service/tenant_sandbox_config.go",
      "summary": "UserEnvService exposed the internal __workspace_scripts_policy__ sentinel TenantSandboxConfig row in ListScopes and accepted user env secrets against its ID, while TenantSandboxConfigService allowed creating a sandbox config named __workspace_scripts_policy__ (colliding with workspace scripts policy storage) and leaked the sentinel row in Inventory.",
      "regression_test": "TestW3BAudit_SandboxWorkspacePolicySentinelRowIsHiddenAndReserved",
      "commit": "7ccf6722d549d5535428d033b3e249902b4bcf80"
    },
    {
      "id": "W3-SVCB-04",
      "severity": "P1",
      "file": "internal/application/service/mcp_service.go",
      "summary": "UpdateMCPService failed to clear AuthConfig.ClientSecret when MCPUpdateDropSecrets was requested, omitted Headers and MCPUpdateDropSecrets from needsReconnect detection, lacked nil s.mcpManager guards on disconnect paths, and TestMCPService omitted caller tenant fallback and MCPOAuthPrincipal propagation for OAuth-backed MCP transports.",
      "regression_test": "TestW3BAudit_MCPService_DropSecretsClearsClientSecretAndTestUsesMCPOAuthPrincipal",
      "commit": "7ccf6722d549d5535428d033b3e249902b4bcf80"
    },
    {
      "id": "W3-SVCB-05",
      "severity": "P1",
      "file": "internal/application/service/message.go",
      "summary": "ClearSessionMessages queried GetKnowledgeIDsBySessionID after DeleteMessagesBySessionID had already deleted the session messages rows (leaving session-uploaded temporary knowledge orphaned on clear), launched cleanup even if message deletion failed, and rerankResults sliced results[rr.Index] without guarding negative provider indices.",
      "regression_test": "TestW3BAudit_ClearSessionMessages_DeletesChatHistoryKBBeforeRowsDisappear",
      "commit": "7ccf6722d549d5535428d033b3e249902b4bcf80"
    },
    {
      "id": "W3-SVCB-06",
      "severity": "P1",
      "file": "internal/application/service/session.go, internal/application/service/session_fork.go",
      "summary": "GenerateTitleAsync passed the caller *types.Session pointer directly into a background goroutine that mutated session.Title concurrently with caller reads/serialization, UpdateSession did not check existing == nil when GetByID returned (nil, nil), and forkOnSharedMachine omitted Kind: source.Kind when persisting forked sessions.",
      "regression_test": "TestW3BAudit_Session_GenerateTitleAsyncRace_UpdateNilGuard_AndSharedForkKind",
      "commit": "7ccf6722d549d5535428d033b3e249902b4bcf80"
    },
    {
      "id": "W3-SVCB-07",
